  "id": "446f4af0-b092-5a11-9050-4ac4598b325f",
  "slug": "mommas-sloppy-joes",
  "name": "Momma's Sloppy Joes",
  "recipe_type": "main",
  "brief_description": "My mom has been making this basic sloppy joe recipe for so long that when I asked her how she made them, she had to make a batch to be sure of the measurements. These are no fancy joes - nothing but lots of sloppy, zesty mess! Beef may be used instead of turkey. Perfect for potluck or game day.",
  "cuisine": "U.S.",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Place the turkey in a large skillet over medium heat, cook until evenly brown, and drain."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "In a large saucepan over medium heat, mix the ketchup, sugar, vinegar, and mustard. Mix in the turkey. Cook, stirring often, 30 minutes."
    }
  ],
